In article <1992Oct9.223242.21140@yenta.alb.nm.us> dt@yenta.alb.nm.us (David B. Thomas) writes:
>I know that pets will initially avoid stepping on cursed items, and that
>you can train them to overcome this fear by throwing food onto a cursed
>item.
>
>My question is: what if your pet kills a monster that is carrying a cursed
>item, and is hungry.  Will the pet pounce on the food, and lose the innate
>fear of cursed items?
>
>						little david

Hungry pets will jump on the pile and eat the corpse, then jump off.
If there is a cursed item there, they don't appear to step back on it.


I did discover one interesting thing about cursed piles and food, though:

I was ready to descend a level, and was trying to get my pet to follow, but
to no avail.  He just wouldn't leave one room, even though there were no
cursed items in the way.  I finally discovered that there was a cursed
tripe ration in the room -- my pet wanted the food, but wouldn't step on
the pile to get the cursed food.  As soon as I picked it up, he was
happy to follow.


